    {
      "content": "The Ferrugal Siphon is a large invertebrate that inhabits grasslands\n and areas of low vegetation. It can exceed five meters in length\nand moves by crawling with undulating motions.",
      "left": "365.5px",
      "top": "194.2px",
      "scale": "2.000000000000001",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "stormgust",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "It is predominantly herbivorous and detritivorous, filtering organic matter and\nhard minerals from the soil through its siphon-shaped mouth apparatus.",
      "left": "326px",
      "top": "317px",
      "scale": "2.000000000000001",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "stormgust",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "Nocturnal and solitary in nature, it remains underground for most of its life,\noccasionally emerging on nights illuminated by blue light. When threatened,\n it expels a viscous fluid with a pungent odor to disorient potential attackers.",
      "left": "300.6px",
      "top": "436.6px",
      "scale": "2.000000000000001",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "stormgust",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    }
